Processes:      htop, ps, kill, nvidia-smi
Services:       systemctl start/stop/restart/status
Disk:           df -h, du -sh
Network:        curl, wget, scp, rsync
Sessions:       tmux new/attach/detach


On a Linux GPU box everything is a process forked from a parent: init spawns sshd, your login spawns bash, bash spawns the training run.
SIGINT from Ctrl-C, or kill against the pid you find with ps aux, ends the leaf and frees its GPU memory, which is how you reclaim a box a dead run is still holding.


